  "predeclared_acceptance": [
    "Use only C03 1.0.2 final staffing-1 -02 and staffing-2 -04 accepted CLI runs. Recompute source contract/evidence/review, published Git and local bytes of all 16 accepted source paths, all input/closure/invocation pins, and every SHA-256/size seal in both 11-file raw maps. Recompute published C03.var01 parent pins. No native execution is authorized.",
    "Compare every authored table, column, instance, row and cell in the two inputs. Their only delta must be ResourceAllocation AIR_BASIC/P-CREW/BASE-01 RQTY 1 versus 2. Keep the same one formation mission, physical aircraft IDs 0 and 1, h7.5 preparation start, one P-CREW request per aircraft and 0.5-hour INSPECT duration.",
    "Confirm each original SSH session 0, sshd ancestry, global mutex, preserved responsive GUI PID 13340 in session 1 with the recorded start identity, four successful import/export/calc/report stages, zero converter errors, warnings exactly #108/#126, notes zero, valid nontrivial SXO and all populated authored cells in each 20 row-containing-table native roundtrip. Do not repeat the runs.",
    "In the one-crew log, require one mission ID to allocate physical aircraft 0 and 1 at h7.5. Aircraft 0's subtask 0 requests, books and performs with P-CREW from h7.5 to h8 while aircraft 1's subtask 1 request fails and waits. Require ordered native h8 lines: subtask 0 completed, frees resources, P-CREW deallocated (available now 1), station triggers waiting tasks and names subtask 1, subtask 1 availability retest succeeds, resource received, books resources, the same P-CREW allocated (available now 0), and subtask 1 starts performing. Require aircraft 1 work h8–8.5, release at h8.5, both preparations complete before joint h8.5 launch; mission success/completion h9.5 and both aircraft ready.",
    "In the two-crew control, require both physical IDs 0 and 1 independently book P-CREW and perform h7.5–8, with two h8 releases, no failed availability test or waiting, joint launch h8, success/completion h9 and both ready. The pair constrains the observed h8 ordering but is not a general scheduling experiment.",
    "Reconcile every cell of ProblemDescription 1x1, ResultSummary 1x11, SystemResults 72x40, StockTotalResults 72x16, ResourceResults 72x16 and ResourceResultsTotal 1x14 in each arm: 5,210 cells per arm. From the physical windows, derive half-hour system ready/preparing/reserved/operating and resource busy/waiting ledgers. Require ProblemDescription, ResultSummary and StockTotalResults equal across arms; exact pair difference counts are 12 SystemResults, 219 ResourceResults and 4 ResourceResultsTotal cells. Common stock has no issue/backorder. ResourceResults.NRA is not a free-worker complement of NRUM.",
    "Require a separately authored standard-library read-only replay before publication. Preserve any review failure and source/raw bytes; do not use an author checker as independent authority."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Retrospective fixed-seed two-run classification of one shared P-CREW pool and a single two-aircraft formation; it overlaps accepted C03.var01 and adds no native run.",
    "The h8 release, retest, regrant and work sequence is a logged observation for these exact physical task and aircraft IDs, not a general same-time scheduling, aircraft-priority, or resource fairness law.",
    "The matched pair changes crew capacity as well as observed launch time; report differences do not isolate a universal causal effect of same-time ordering.",
    "No equipment shortage, shifts, alternate formations, faults, other seeds, GUI-only behavior, cross-engine parity or full C03/Issue18 completion claim."
  ]
}
